# SCP (Secure Copy)
- Used to transfer files between systems using SSH

## Capabilities
- Local → Remote copy
- Remote → Local copy

## Examples
- scp file user@IP:/paths
- scp user@IP:/path files


# Python HTTP Server
- Module: http.server
- Used to create simple web server

## Start Server
- python3 -m http.server

## Notes
- Runs on port 8000 by default
- Serves files from current directory

## Download Example
- wget http://MACHINE_IP:8000/file


# Processes
- Programs running on system
- Managed by kernel
- Each process has PID (Process ID)


# Viewing Processes
- ps → shows running processes
- ps aux → shows all processes


# Top Command
- Shows real-time process statistics
- Updates automatically

## Displays
- CPU usage
- Memory usage
- Running processes


# Managing Processes
- kill command → terminate process
- Syntax: kill PID

## Signals
- SIGTERM → graceful stop
- SIGKILL → force stop
- SIGSTOP → pause process


# Process Creation
- OS uses namespace to manage resources
- Helps isolate processes
- Improves security


# systemd
- First process started (PID 1)
- Manages other processes
- All programs run as child processes of systemd


# systemctl Command
- Used to interact with systemd

## Syntax
- systemctl [option] [service]

## Common Options
- start → start service
- stop → stop service
- enable → start on boot
- disable → prevent start on boot
- status → check status

## Example
- systemctl start apache2


# Foreground and Background Processes

## Foreground
- Runs in terminal
- Output shown immediately

## Background
- Runs without blocking terminal
- Use & to run in background

## Example
- echo "Hi TTM" &

## Process Control
- Ctrl + Z → suspend process (send to background)

## Foregrounding
- fg → bring process to foreground
